Advanced islanding, black start and restoration (@pe-restoration-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC", #source "../sources/Commissioning-Guide-Hydroelectric-FIST.lingua#r_0WA7RR86PMVEA3FFM7CG6NQ5RM", #source "../sources/Grid-Forming-Inverters-Research-Roadmap.lingua#r_1XBSV4CPJGZG5FE56MH7507WAF", #source "../sources/UNIFI-Grid-Forming-Specifications-Version-2.lingua#r_5SF91JRQ8TE46HXTXRK16P9KBZ", #electrical-power-engineering "../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3") { r_7MACDJMFMNF4HV4MRV56A33JNP
**Read:** [Conduct of power operations and maintenance — FIST](../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC), both whole manuals and complete applicable procedures; [Commissioning Guide for Hydroelectric Facilities — FIST 4-7](../sources/Commissioning-Guide-Hydroelectric-FIST.lingua#r_0WA7RR86PMVEA3FFM7CG6NQ5RM), entire relevant integration/commissioning context; [Research Roadmap on Grid-Forming Inverters](../sources/Grid-Forming-Inverters-Research-Roadmap.lingua#r_1XBSV4CPJGZG5FE56MH7507WAF), complete applicable model and source-capability discussion; [UNIFI grid-forming specifications, version 2](../sources/UNIFI-Grid-Forming-Specifications-Version-2.lingua#r_5SF91JRQ8TE46HXTXRK16P9KBZ), whole relevant functional specification.

Read the complete applicable [Conduct of power operations and maintenance — FIST](../sources/Conduct-of-Power-Operations-and-Maintenance-FIST.lingua#r_4JS2N9S01A3KTMH37TXMVSPPYC) and [Commissioning Guide for Hydroelectric Facilities — FIST 4-7](../sources/Commissioning-Guide-Hydroelectric-FIST.lingua#r_0WA7RR86PMVEA3FFM7CG6NQ5RM) material, all relevant [Research Roadmap on Grid-Forming Inverters](../sources/Grid-Forming-Inverters-Research-Roadmap.lingua#r_1XBSV4CPJGZG5FE56MH7507WAF)/[UNIFI grid-forming specifications, version 2](../sources/UNIFI-Grid-Forming-Specifications-Version-2.lingua#r_5SF91JRQ8TE46HXTXRK16P9KBZ) methods and the actual connection/operation requirements. Choose a documented bounded system with explicit sources, auxiliary energy, controls/protection, loads and energization paths.

Derive a sequence from a known initial state through forming supply, auxiliary startup, line/transformer energization, load pickup, additional sources and any resynchronization. Model time-dependent voltage/frequency, inrush/current limits, stored energy, reactive demand and protection rather than checking only the final load flow. Include both synchronous and converter-based alternatives where the actual source data support them.

Compare analytical/numerical limits with a complete public or suitable qualified physical case. Test a changed auxiliary, failed communication or unavailable source and predict the revised service/restoration time. Preserve intermediate state, settings and evidence and distinguish a simulated sequence from demonstrated operating capability. The finished study should explain why nominal spare MW or a source labelled black start is insufficient without its supporting material, control, human and energy system.

**Continue:** [An integrated electrical-power-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
